GrUBI Registry

	Philosophy

		-
			A GrUBI registry is a publication of a series of anonymous recipient profiles, each
			with a series of payment endpoint options specifying currency type and public payment
			addresses.
			
			Each recipient profile shall have a unique ID, and may have an indefinite number of
			tags so as to denote, among other things, group memberships and verification status.

			A GrUBI registry should ideally be implemented as a plain text file in a data
			interchange format, and published online at a publicly accessible URL.
		-

	Principles

		GrUBI JSON

			-
				GrUBI JSON is a JSON format for implementing GrUBI registries.

				A GrUBI JSON registry consists of a list of GrUBI objects, each representing a
				recipient profile.

				A GrUBI JSON object shall have the field "properties", containing an object which
				contains all other data.

				The properties object shall have the field "ID", containing a string specifying a
				unique ID for that profile.

				The properties object shall have the field "tags", containing a string list, with
				each string specifying a tag assigned to that profile.

				The properties object shall have the field "endpoints", containing a list of
				endpoint objects, each specifying a payment endpoint for that profile.

				An endpoint object shall have the field "currency", containing a string specifying
				the currency code for that endpoint.

				An endpoint object shall have the field "address", a string specifying the public
				wallet address for that endpoint.

				For traditional currency sent via a payment processor, the address shall take the
				form of a string in the GrUBI processor address format, which begins with the root
				URL of the payment processor's main website, followed by the '@' symbol, followed
				by the recipient's username on said payment processor.
			-